  "concept": {
    "movement": "A broad, heavy four-beat trundle with full alternating steps, quiet barrel torso and visible upper-leg drive. Faster travel is a purposeful low trot with no flight; the short centered tail follows the rump coherently.",
    "attack": "A brief backward brace loads the massive shoulders, then a forceful forward head-and-shoulder shove drives through a forefoot landing. The source closed muzzle stays coherent, with no unsupported jaw-opening deformation.",
    "death": "The head lowers as the knees fold, then the heavy barrel settles onto a supported flank. Released paws relax with native section lengths while skull, chest and pelvis remain close to the ground in a still final hold."
